-# Design analysis for the D9 variant.
-#
-# a) Concretization and trace:
-#    - The original task stamps a full 3x3 opposite-color patch around each black dent.
-#      Near a region boundary, that square can spill into black background or the other
-#      foreground region.
-#    - In this variant the dent still belongs to one host region, but after the 3x3 patch
-#      is generated it is clipped by the host region mask. Only cells that were part of
-#      that host foreground region survive; the rest remain unchanged. The teal center is
-#      still written afterward.
-#    - Example: if a dent sits one cell inside an L-shaped corner, the original output
-#      produces a solid 3x3 square crossing the corner; the variant keeps only the subset
-#      of that square lying inside the host region, so the patch becomes an L or T shape.
-#
-# b) Complexity calibration:
-#    - The rule stays single-step and local: clean noise, detect dents, stamp opposite
-#      color, mark teal. The only new operation is host-region clipping.
-#    - To keep the change visible, the generator requires multiple dents whose 3x3 patch
-#      would lose cells under clipping. Interior dents are still present as controls.
-#
-# c) Hidden assumption review for main():
-#    - The old line assigning `out[r-1:r+2, c-1:c+2] = other` assumes every in-bounds
